{"reference":"Psalms 107","book":"Psalms","chapter":107,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Psalm’s Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"One disputed way of hearing this psalm places its repeated thanksgiving for rescue and its opening picture of people gathered from many lands alongside Book V’s wider themes of return thanksgiving, festival praise, and worship. This setting can deepen the force of the communal call for the redeemed to speak of God’s enduring lovingkindness.","verse_refs":["Psalms 107:1-43"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_107_399c02d69436d5558cbf8b54"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}